{"version":"bsb","book":"psalms","chapter":90,"blocks":[{"kind":"heading","level":1,"text":"BOOK IV"},{"kind":"title","text":"Psalms 90–106"},{"kind":"heading","level":2,"text":"From Everlasting to Everlasting"},{"kind":"title","text":"A prayer of Moses the man of God."},{"kind":"break"},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":1,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"Lord, You have been our dwelling place"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":1,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"through all generations."}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":2,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"Before the mountains were born"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":2,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"or You brought forth the earth and the world,"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":2,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"from everlasting to everlasting"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":2,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"You are God."}]},{"kind":"break"},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":3,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"You return man to dust,"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":3,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"saying, “Return, O sons of mortals.”"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":4,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"For in Your sight a thousand years"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":4,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"are but a day that passes,"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":4,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"or a watch of the night."}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":5,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"You sweep them away in their sleep;"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":5,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"they are like the new grass of the morning—"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":6,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"in the morning it springs up new,"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":6,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"but by evening it fades and withers."}]},{"kind":"break"},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":7,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"For we are consumed by Your anger"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":7,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"and terrified by Your wrath."}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":8,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"You have set our iniquities before You,"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":8,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"our secret sins in the light of Your presence."}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":9,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"For all our days decline in Your fury;"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":9,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"we finish our years with a sigh."}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":10,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"The length of our days is seventy years —"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":10,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"or eighty if we are strong —"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":10,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"yet their pride is but labor and sorrow,"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":10,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"for they quickly pass, and we fly away."}]},{"kind":"break"},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":11,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"Who knows the power of Your anger?"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":11,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"Your wrath matches the fear You are due."}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":12,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"So teach us to number our days,"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":12,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"that we may present a heart of wisdom."}]},{"kind":"break"},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":13,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"Return, O LORD! How long will it be?"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":13,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"Have compassion on Your servants."}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":14,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"Satisfy us in the morning with Your loving devotion,"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":14,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"that we may sing for joy and be glad all our days."}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":15,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"Make us glad for as many days as You have afflicted us,"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":15,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"for as many years as we have seen evil."}]},{"kind":"break"},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":16,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"May Your work be shown to Your servants,"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":16,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"and Your splendor to their children."}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":17,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"May the favor of the Lord our God rest upon us;"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":17,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"establish for us the work of our hands—"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":17,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"yes, establish the work of our hands!"}]}]}
